In three/animation/spins.ts: move `allowsChangeOfEdge` and `allowsEight` (lines 547-549) up above `spinTimeline` (near the SpinPhase helpers), and change the marker at line 286-287 to keep the marker but word it by whether the feature counts:

```ts
if (phase.basic && phase.revolutions >= 8) {
  const detail = allowsEight(phase)
    ? "at least eight revolutions without any change of position, variation, foot or edge: a level feature (once per program)"
    : "eight revolutions held without any change, but the feature only counts in a camel, a layback or a difficult variation of a basic position";
  markers.push({ t: from + trans + 8 / rate, label: `${phase.label} · 8 revolutions`, detail });
}
```

Add to tests/spins.test.ts (the "holds eight revolutions…" case): `expect(spinTimeline(spinFromSpec("SSp", { eightRevolutions: true })).markers.find((m) => m.label.endsWith("8 revolutions"))!.detail).not.toMatch(/level feature/)` and the matching positive assertion for CSp (`toMatch(/level feature/)`), so the HUD and `spinFeatureNotes` can no longer diverge.

In three/animation/spins.ts spinTimeline, branch the marker detail on allowsEight instead of dropping the marker, so the hold is still annotated but the HUD agrees with the panel:

```ts
if (phase.basic && phase.revolutions >= 8) {
  const credited = allowsEight(phase);
  markers.push({
    t: from + trans + 8 / rate,
    label: `${phase.label} · 8 revolutions`,
    detail: credited
      ? "at least eight revolutions without any change of position, variation, foot or edge: a level feature (once per program)"
      : "eight revolutions held without any change, but the feature counts only in a camel, a layback or a difficult variation of a basic position",
  });
}
```

Move the `allowsChangeOfEdge` / `allowsEight` consts above `spinTimeline` (optional, there is no TDZ issue since they are only referenced at call time, but it keeps the helper near its first use). Add to tests/spins.test.ts "holds eight revolutions..." test: `expect(spinTimeline(spinFromSpec("SSp", { eightRevolutions: true })).markers.find((m) => m.label.endsWith("8 revolutions"))!.detail).not.toMatch(/a level feature/)` and `.toMatch(/counts only in a camel/)`, and keep the existing CSp assertion as the positive case.
